{
  "_comment": [
    "Canned POST /security/runHuntingQuery responses.",
    "",
    "Each entry has a 'match' array of lowercase substrings. The mock server",
    "lowercases the incoming Query and returns the first entry whose substrings",
    "ALL appear. That is deliberately crude - it is a fixture matcher, not a KQL",
    "engine. Add entries as your agent learns new queries.",
    "",
    "The 'response' object is the real huntingQueryResults shape: a 'schema'",
    "array of {name,type} and a 'results' array of row objects keyed by column",
    "name.",
    "",
    "TABLE AVAILABILITY - this is the part that bites in a real tenant:",
    "  SigninLogs, AuditLogs       Sentinel Analytics-tier tables. Reachable from",
    "                              advanced hunting ONLY when the workspace is",
    "                              onboarded to the Defender portal, and only",
    "                              inside the Analytics retention window.",
    "  CloudAppEvents, IdentityInfo  Native Defender XDR tables. Always available",
    "                              with ThreatHunting.Read.All.",
    "  BehaviorAnalytics           Sentinel UEBA. Analytics tier, same caveat as",
    "                              SigninLogs.",
    "",
    "Synthetic data. No real tenant, no real people."
  ],

